*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
*      PARMS -- machine-dependent constants for the Go SIL machine
*
*      S4D58 6.20 lists thirteen names that this segment must supply.
*      They are all EQU, so PARMS is pure assembly-time text and needs
*      nothing outside SIL to express.
*
*      The choices here follow PLAN.md's core model: Core is a slice of
*      cells, one cell per address unit, and a cell carries a whole
*      descriptor.  Every appearance of DESCR in the SNOBOL4 source is
*      linear -- k*DESCR, label-label-DESCR, DESCR+SPEC, -2*DESCR,
*      DESCR*OBOFF -- with no masking, division or alignment, so DESCR
*      may be any positive integer.  One makes "cell" and "descriptor"
*      the same thing, which S4D58 3.1.1 licenses: "Descriptors do not
*      have to address individual characters of strings."
*
*      CSTACK and OSTACK are the other two names 6.20 mentions.  They
*      are machine registers here rather than storage locations, which
*      6.20 explicitly allows, so they are VM state and not symbols.
*      The SNOBOL4 source never names either one.
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
*
*      Sizes
*
DESCR  EQU     1		   Address width of a descriptor
SPEC   EQU     2		   Address width of a specifier
CPA    EQU     1		   Characters per addressing unit
ALPHSZ EQU     256		   Characters in the character set
SIZLIM EQU     16777215 	   Largest integer in a value field
*
*      Descriptor flags (S4D58 3.1.2).  Five flags are used by SNOBOL4
*      and they are combined by addition -- TTL+MARK, DESCR+SPEC -- so
*      each has to be a distinct bit.
*
TTL    EQU     1		   Title of a block
MARK   EQU     2		   Marked title
PTR    EQU     4		   Points into dynamic storage
FNC    EQU     8		   Function descriptor
STTL   EQU     16		   Title of a string structure
*
*      FORTRAN unit reference numbers (S4D58 2.1).  Kept at the IBM
*      System/360 values; the host interface maps them to streams.
*
UNITI  EQU     5		   Standard input
UNITO  EQU     6		   Standard print output
UNITP  EQU     7		   Standard punch output
*
*      Syntax table action codes (S4D58 4.2).  These are the values of
*      the indicator field T of a syntax table entry, and they reach
*      the machine as the KEY operand of CLERTB and PLUGTB.  CONTIN is
*      zero because 6.19's figure for CLERTB CONTIN shows the indicator
*      field cleared and the address field set to the table itself;
*      the other three are distinct nonzero tags.
*
CONTIN EQU     0		   Continue with the current table
STOP   EQU     1		   Stop, last character included
STOPSH EQU     2		   Stop, last character not included
ERROR  EQU     3		   Stop with an error indication
